  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The magnetic field B crossing normally a square metallic plate of area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is changing with time as shown in figure. The magnitude of induced emf in the plate during <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>V</mi></math>.</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5d6c8bc7-7667-4b17-8b7e-ef248b88dcf4-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 193px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5d6c8bc7-7667-4b17-8b7e-ef248b88dcf4-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 193px;\" /></p><p>From the graph, it can be seen that the value of the magnetic field at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mT</mi></math>, whereas the magnetic field at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mT</mi></math>.</p><p>The formula to calculate the magnitude of the induced emf is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mtext>ind&#160;</mtext></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>A</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is the slope of the given graph.</p><p>Hence, the value of the induced emf can be calculated as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnspacing=\"0px\" columnalign=\"right center left\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mtext>ind&#160;</mtext></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mT</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mT</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mV</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>",
